      "body": [
        "Arize Phoenix is an open-source AI observability tool that calculates model-call costs from recorded token usage and model prices. Its built-in pricing catalog previously changed with server releases. A missing or outdated rate therefore required an upgrade or custom configuration. Automatic catalog updates let the server receive revised prices between upgrades.",
        "Shortly after startup, and then about daily, the server downloads a catalog published in the Phoenix GitHub repository from LiteLLM pricing data. It compares catalog generation dates and saves newer model entries and prices in one database transaction. Deployments sharing PostgreSQL use a database lock so only one server applies an update at a time. A saved catalog record prevents an older bundled catalog from overwriting downloaded prices after restart.",
